                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I feel bad not recommending a game that's free that the dev clearly cared about, but even for 2017 this kinda sucks and i don't think it is worth your time. both then and now have examples of this for free done much better.\n\nthe droning (in a bad way) basic repetitive sad sack piano tracks make the whole thing feel like z grade victorian poems, and its clearly trying to add weight and atmosphere to a game that has none of it. it's dark and hard to see anything, but not because of performance or imposed darkness, there's just nothing there but untextured brown walls. theres basic platforming in it because... well i dont know why.\n\nthe first puzzle is an easy puzzle presented in the most confusing on purpose way possible that its impossible to take seriously in a game that, again, REALLY wants you to feel like you are in some dark surreal dour situation when it just feels like youre in Tron's shittiest house. there are no options to tweak mouse sensitivity, so its brutal to turn, and naturally your cursor goes off window all the time making you click out of the game if you have a two monitor setup.\n\nspeaking of, the options for me anyway, were reversed, so i actually had to select left monitor to show it on my right and vice versa. thats a new one. add to that really finicky unresponsive and/or badly placed interactive stuff and hotspots like... dude just dont play it. i feel bad but seriously the game isn't offensive or anything it just sucks.",
